-- title:
--   Decode every scalar field in its stored order.
-- statement:
--   Decode every scalar field in its stored order. The input packet length
--   in address register 37 is unchanged and the final cursor identifies its end.
--   Only scratch address registers 3 through 6, 11 and 12 are touched, so all VM
--   state in the high address bank is preserved.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.SignWire.wordSignFragment_rawReply_capture`.
